    "player_hint_1_en": "(C) cannot be the woman beside the crate with (B) in the Boathouse because she has to be east of (A). (B) and the woman beside a crate in his area cannot be in R3 and R4 because that would limit (F) to be in R2. This would only leave one boat available, which won't fit both (A) and (C). This means that (B) and the unknown woman must be in the Fish Market or Warehouse.",
    "player_hint_2_en": "Who can be the woman with (B)? It can only be (D). It cannot be (C) because she's on a boat. It cannot be (E) because there are no chairs beside a crate. It cannot be (V) because she must be alone with the murderer, and we know that (D) is in the Fish Market, and (H) is in the Warehouse, so (B) and (V) wouldn't be alone. This means (D) must be in R8. Cross out the rest of the row.",
    "player_hint_3_en": "Amongst R7 - R9, (H) is in the Warehouse beside a shelf, and (B) and (D) are in the Fish Market. This means all three rows are occupied. Cross out the Boardwalk squares in R7.",
    "player_hint_4_en": "Because (H) has to be in C7 or C8, that means the boat in R2 cannot be empty. (C) must be in this boat since she is east of (A). Block out the rest of R2.",
    "player_hint_5_en": "This narrows (F) and (G) to R3 and R4. (G) cannot occupy the boat in the Boathouse because one boat out of the three is entirely inside the two empty columns, and (A) must be in the second boat. This means the boat in the Boathouse is empty. Cross out all squares in C2 and C3.",
    "player_hint_6_en": "This isolates (A) to R1 C4. This isolates (D) and (B) and then (H). This isolates (C).",
    "player_hint_7_en": "This isolates (E) to the last chair on the Boardwalk. This isolates (G) then (F). (V) takes the last square on the Boardwalk with (E). Erin is the murderer!"
  },
